            <ArticleTitle>[Pharmacotherapy for obesity].</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">V06160406</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity is a chronic condition, which is why pharmacotherapy can be considered, if lifestyle modification (hypocaloric diet/exercise) does not result in a weight loss of at least 5%. Pharmacotherapy is indicated, if an individual has a BMI &gt; 30 kg/m(2) or a BMI &gt; 27 kg/m(2) and concomitant disease (e.g. Type 2 diabetes), and can be liraglutide (3 mg) or orlistat (120 mg/60 mg). Choice of treatment must be based on patient preferences and clinical situation, side effects, contraindications and financial considerations. Weight loss of &lt; 5% (about 4-5 kg) after 12 weeks should lead to cessation of the treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
